# Use public APIs, not workarounds

Before changing colors, layout, widgets, or framework behavior, read how that library is supposed to do it. Use that API. Do not invent a local patch, then "fix" it when it fails.

## Do this

1. Find the first-class API (docs, crate source, or existing project usage).
2. Implement with that API.
3. If it still fails, you used it wrong or the version differs. Re-read. Do not paper over it.

## Do not do this

- Mutate whatever object is in reach (`set_style` on the active style, hardcoded colors on one widget, extra draw calls) because it looks faster.
- Stamp the same values onto every code path so an official switch cannot fire.
- Re-apply a setting every frame to beat framework defaults.
- Promise a process change in chat. Put it in a rule or just do the work.

## Example (egui 0.31)

```rust
// Wrong: writes the current style only. System light theme replaces it next frame.
ctx.set_style(style);

// Right: custom palette lives on the dark theme; then select that theme.
ctx.set_visuals_of(egui::Theme::Dark, dark_blue_visuals());
ctx.set_theme(egui::Theme::Dark);
```

Shared spacing/fonts go through `all_styles_mut`. Theme colors go on `Theme::Dark` / `Theme::Light`. Theme selection is `set_theme`.
